---
id: react-native
title: Usage with React Native
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Form is headless, so React Native uses the same form and validation\nAPIs. Connect the field handlers to the props exposed by native controls."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Button, Text, TextInput, View } from 'react-native'\nimport { useForm } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nexport function AccountForm() {\n  const form = useForm({\n    defaultValues: { age: '' },\n    onSubmit: ({ value }) => console.log(value),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <View>\n      <form.Field\n        name=\"age\"\n        validators={[\n          {\n            triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n            run: ({ value }) =>\n              Number(value) >= 13 ? undefined : 'You must be at least 13',\n          },\n        ]}\n      >\n        {(field) => (\n          <View>\n            <Text>Age</Text>\n            <TextInput\n              value={field.value}\n              keyboardType=\"number-pad\"\n              onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n              onChangeText={field.handleChange}\n            />\n            {field.errors.map((error) => (\n              <Text key={error.message} accessibilityRole=\"alert\">\n                {error.message}\n              </Text>\n            ))}\n          </View>\n        )}\n      </form.Field>\n\n      <Button title=\"Submit\" onPress={() => void form.handleSubmit()} />\n    </View>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React Native has no DOM form submission or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"querySelector"},{"type":"text","value":". Call\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.handleSubmit()"},{"type":"text","value":" from a button and keep refs to native inputs when you need\nto focus an invalid field."}]}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Form is headless, so React Native uses the same form and validation\nAPIs. Connect the field handlers to the props exposed by native controls.\n\n```tsx\nimport { Button, Text, TextInput, View } from 'react-native'\nimport { useForm } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nexport function AccountForm() {\n  const form = useForm({\n    defaultValues: { age: '' },\n    onSubmit: ({ value }) => console.log(value),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <View>\n      <form.Field\n        name=\"age\"\n        validators={[\n          {\n            triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n            run: ({ value }) =>\n              Number(value) >= 13 ? undefined : 'You must be at least 13',\n          },\n        ]}\n      >\n        {(field) => (\n          <View>\n            <Text>Age</Text>\n            <TextInput\n              value={field.value}\n              keyboardType=\"number-pad\"\n              onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n              onChangeText={field.handleChange}\n            />\n            {field.errors.map((error) => (\n              <Text key={error.message} accessibilityRole=\"alert\">\n                {error.message}\n              </Text>\n            ))}\n          </View>\n        )}\n      </form.Field>\n\n      <Button title=\"Submit\" onPress={() => void form.handleSubmit()} />\n    </View>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nReact Native has no DOM form submission or `querySelector`. Call\n`form.handleSubmit()` from a button and keep refs to native inputs when you need\nto focus an invalid field.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: react-native\ntitle: Usage with React Native\n---\n\nTanStack Form is headless, so React Native uses the same form and validation\nAPIs. Connect the field handlers to the props exposed by native controls.\n\n```tsx\nimport { Button, Text, TextInput, View } from 'react-native'\nimport { useForm } from '@tanstack/react-form'\n\nexport function AccountForm() {\n  const form = useForm({\n    defaultValues: { age: '' },\n    onSubmit: ({ value }) => console.log(value),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <View>\n      <form.Field\n        name=\"age\"\n        validators={[\n          {\n            triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n            run: ({ value }) =>\n              Number(value) >= 13 ? undefined : 'You must be at least 13',\n          },\n        ]}\n      >\n        {(field) => (\n          <View>\n            <Text>Age</Text>\n            <TextInput\n              value={field.value}\n              keyboardType=\"number-pad\"\n              onBlur={field.handleBlur}\n              onChangeText={field.handleChange}\n            />\n            {field.errors.map((error) => (\n              <Text key={error.message} accessibilityRole=\"alert\">\n                {error.message}\n              </Text>\n            ))}\n          </View>\n        )}\n      </form.Field>\n\n      <Button title=\"Submit\" onPress={() => void form.handleSubmit()} />\n    </View>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nReact Native has no DOM form submission or `querySelector`. Call\n`form.handleSubmit()` from a button and keep refs to native inputs when you need\nto focus an invalid field.\n"}
